---
import Drawing from "../components/Drawing.astro";
import VideoFrame from "../components/VideoFrame.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { studio } from "../data/site";
---

<Base
	title="About Mr. Shahnawaz, architect since 1996"
	description="Mr. Shahnawaz has practised architecture since 1996. The studio designs jewelry showrooms, residences, and banquet halls, and still begins each room on paper."
	image="/posters/residence.jpg"
>
	<div class="wrap page">
		<header class="page-title">
			<h1>About</h1>
			<p>
				{studio.principal} has practised architecture since {studio.since}. The
				studio is the work of that practice: showrooms, houses, and halls.
			</p>
		</header>

		<div class="split">
			<VideoFrame film="residence" eager />
			<div class="stack measure">
				<p>
					The rooms are commercial and domestic at once. A jewelry showroom
					has to sell and still feel calm. A house has to hold a joint family
					without making every hour a corridor. A banquet hall has to carry a
					wedding from the car to the last table.
				</p>
				<p>
					He draws before he specifies. Clients see a plan and a section, and
					they can point to the place where an elder sits, where a necklace is
					lifted from the case, or where the kitchen door must not appear in
					a photograph.
				</p>
				<p>
					The studio stays with the site. A drawing that cannot be built in
					the order a contractor actually works is sent back to the sheet.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<section class="section measure">
			<h2>How a room is decided</h2>
			<p>
				Three questions come first. Who stops in this room, and for how long.
				Where does the light need to fall. What must stay out of sight: a
				store, a kitchen, a stair, a safe. Finishes follow those answers.
				Brass appears where the hand meets a case or a rail. Plaster and stone
				do the larger surfaces.
			</p>
			<p>
				If you are bringing a site, a family house, or a hall that already
				stands, write with the day the room has to hold. The studio will reply
				with questions before a fee.
			</p>
			<p class="actions">
				<a class="button" href="/contact">Start a conversation</a>
				<a href="/services">See the services</a>
			</p>
		</section>

		<div class="drawing-row three section">
			<Drawing kind="stair" label="Section through a stair" />
			<Drawing kind="pavilion" label="Front of a showroom" />
			<Drawing kind="hall" label="Section through a banquet hall" />
		</div>
	</div>
</Base>
